<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB leaves ASW pool price steady at A$175/t.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB leaves ASW pool price steady at A$175/t.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) left its estimated 1996/97 pool price for benchmark Australian Standard White (ASW) wheat unchanged at A$175.00 a tonne and slightly increased prices on some other grades.</p>
<p>Prime Hard, Durum 1, Durum 2 and feedwheat were all increased in price by A$5.00 a tonne while other pool prices were left unchanged, AWB said.</p>
